From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:56:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: let the firmware probe unload with the core
 module

The firmware probe registered with builtin_platform_driver(), which in
a module gives an init without an exit, so mt6797-wlan-core loaded as
permanent and could never be unloaded. Register it as an ordinary
module platform driver; its only resource is device-managed.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/firmware-probe.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/firmware-probe.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/firmware-probe.c
index b848e6f24..e7293f5f0 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/firmware-probe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/firmware-probe.c
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /* Passive MT6797 WLAN firmware probe below the shared CONSYS owner. */
 
 #include <linux/errno.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 
@@ -57,4 +58,4 @@ static struct platform_driver mt6797_wlan_firmware_driver = {
 		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
 	},
 };
-builtin_platform_driver(mt6797_wlan_firmware_driver);
+module_platform_driver(mt6797_wlan_firmware_driver);
-- 
2.43.0

